From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wintab32: manager cursor settings and packet hooks (3652)

wintab32: manager cursor settings and packet hooks

WTMgrCsrEnable, WTMgrCsrButtonMap, WTMgrCsrPressureBtnMarks(Ex) and
WTMgrCsrPressureResponse store per-cursor settings that are applied to every packet
before it is queued and reported by WTInfo; WTMgrPacketHookEx/Unhook/HookNext run
record hooks on every packet. WTMgrDeviceConfig stays a stub (driver dialog).
---
